27.5% of the higher of remuneration (as defined in paragraph 1 of the Fourth Schedule) and taxable income, each excluding retirement fund lump sum benefits, retirement fund lump sum withdrawal benefits and severance benefits, with taxable income determined before the s 11F and s 18A deductions; a taxable capital gain is included in this taxable income (s 11F(2)(b));
taxable income determined before the s 11F deduction and before the inclusion of any taxable capital gain (s 11F(2)(c)). This third limit is the taxable income itself, not 27.5% of it.
Contributions above the limit carry forward to the next year of assessment and are deemed to be contributed in that year.
